<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Once a day, just after midnight: snapshot the vocabulary data into git. See
  lib/vocab/backup.py.

  **Why 00:05 and not the 21:00 it used to share with publish.** The weekly report runs
  on a separate host since 2026-08-03 and reads *this* snapshot (`gigaku report
  --from-backup`), not the live cache. Its window is the last complete calendar week,
  Monday–Sunday, so a Sunday-21:00 snapshot cut the reported week three hours short — and
  those words were lost for good, not deferred: their mod date falls in the week just
  reported, so the *next* week's window skips them too. A snapshot taken after midnight
  contains the whole of the day it is snapshotting, which is what a daily backup should
  have meant all along.

  Five past, not on the hour: nothing here races the date rollover, and the machine has
  enough else firing at exactly 00:00.

  This has to run on the Mac and cannot move: it reads Migaku's list out of Chrome's
  IndexedDB and the AnkiMorphs CSVs out of the Anki profile, both local. Chrome does NOT
  need to be running — `_chrome_rows` reads the blob off disk and inflates it into a temp
  SQLite — and at this hour it is more likely to have flushed than at nine in the evening.

  Pushing works unattended only with an ssh key the agent can use without a prompt. A
  missed run (Mac asleep) fires on the next wake. A failed or stale backup alerts Telegram
  itself (lib/vocab/backup.py), and the report host's Monday job additionally checks how
  old words.json is before it reports on it.

  Install:  cp launchd/com.gigaku.backup.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
            launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.gigaku.backup.plist
  Run now:  launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.gigaku.backup
  Log:      /tmp/gigaku-backup.log
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>com.gigaku.backup</string>
	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>/bin/sh</string>
		<string>-c</string>
		<string>/Users/USERNAME/.local/bin/gigaku backup</string>
	</array>
	<key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
	<dict>
		<key>Hour</key>
		<integer>0</integer>
		<key>Minute</key>
		<integer>5</integer>
	</dict>
	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<false/>
	<key>ProcessType</key>
	<string>Background</string>
	<key>StandardOutPath</key>
	<string>/tmp/gigaku-backup.log</string>
	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>/tmp/gigaku-backup.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
